{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgXjYBD8n6Aa9cszQcfDZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] AGENTS.md states the tapout port-collision rule twice\n\nI fixed both findings in two separate commits.\n\n1. **Swap test (`test/index.ts`):** I removed the assertion that couldn't fail. The test now checks two things after an app button swap: the replacement inner button has no `aria-label`, and `el.ariaLabel` is `null`. To prove the new check can fail, I briefly changed the getter to return the stored label. The suite then reported `not ok 107`. I put `src/client.ts` back afterwards.\n2. **AGENTS.md:** I removed the port rule (tapout's fixed port and the `EADDRINUSE` advice) from \"Button tests\" and kept the copy in \"Running the browser suite\". I also added a short note to \"Button tests\" on that check: break the code briefly in `src/` and see the test fail.\n\nThe full `npm test` first exited with code 127. The CSS build tool in `node_modules` was still an uninstalled placeholder, the problem AGENTS.md already describes. I ran the documented fix (`node postinstall.js` in `node_modules/lightningcss-cli`). After that, `npm test` passes all 108 tests and lint is clean.\n\nEverything is committed. Notes are in `.nightralph/notes.md`, which is uncommitted as instructed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":430,"cache_read_input_tokens":48429,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":430},"output_tokens":431,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a75bbcae-f304-4171-89dc-e53ff3f3fafb","uuid":"c6825f21-17ea-4c11-b8d7-881ddd9029fe","timestamp":"2026-10-30T03:45:36.087Z","request_id":"req_011CgXjYAu26RC8vQCth6Fdr"}
